Now let me also improve `chunkForSsml` while I'm here — it has a subtle bug: `chunks += part.trim()` but then `rest.delete(0, part.length)` — `part` was possibly cut at '&' — handled. But if `take <= 0` → `take = limit` — could then `rest.substring(0, take)` throw if rest shorter? substring(0, take) with take > length throws... Actually the loop `while (take > 0)` decrements take only on non-whole-utf8 which never happens — so take stays `limit`. If `rest.length < limit` — but we early-return when whole text ≤ limit. So rest.length > limit always at loop start... not exactly: after several chunks rest could become ≤ limit — then the early-return check at next function call doesn't happen (it's a loop, not recursion). `rest.substring(0, take)` with take=limit > rest.length → IndexOutOfBounds! Wait: `rest.substring(0, limit)` — Kotlin throws StringIndexOutOfBoundsException if limit > length. Let me check: first iteration rest > limit guaranteed. Part consumed → rest decreases. Eventually rest.length could be < limit at the start of a while iteration → crash!

Example: text of exactly 4100 bytes with limit 4000: first take=4000 (whole utf8 immediately) → part = 4000 chars, rest = 100 chars. Loop: rest not empty → take = limit (4000) → candidate = rest.substring(0, 4000) → StringIndexOutOfBoundsException!

Hmm wait — the initial check: `if (text.toByteArray().size <= limit) return listOf(text)` — 4100 > 4000 so we enter loop. First chunk: take=4000 → candidate = rest.substring(0,4000) OK (rest is 4100). isWholeUtf8 → true → break. part = rest.substring(0, 4000). amp check. chunks += part.trim() — trim may reduce length. rest.delete(0, part.length) → rest = 100 chars (approximately). Loop again: rest.isNotEmpty() → take = limit = 4000 → candidate = rest.substring(0, 4000) with rest.length=100 → **StringIndexOutOfBoundsException**. BUG! Catastrophic for long texts (>4000 bytes): speakEdge would throw → caught by synthesizeToFile's catch → returns null → fallback to system TTS (so not a crash, but Edge voice silently breaks for any text > 4KB).

Fix: `var take = minOf(limit, rest.length)`.

Also `rest.delete(0, part.length)` — part was derived from rest.substring(0, take) so part.length == take ≤ rest.length — OK.

Also the `isWholeUtf8` check is useless as analyzed (always true for valid UTF-16 strings). Actually not exactly: unpaired surrogates would round-trip differently, but in practice it's a no-op. Keep it harmless — but I could simplify: take = min(limit, rest.length). Keep the loop as is otherwise.

Let me fix chunkForSsml:

```kotlin
    internal fun chunkForSsml(text: String, limit: Int = SSML_BYTE_LIMIT): List<String> {
        if (text.toByteArray(Charsets.UTF_8).size <= limit) return listOf(text)
        val chunks = mutableListOf<String>()
        val rest = StringBuilder(text)
        while (rest.isNotEmpty()) {
            var take = minOf(limit, rest.length)
            while (take > 0) {
                val candidate = rest.substring(0, take)
                if (candidate.isWholeUtf8()) break
                take--
            }
            if (take <= 0) take = minOf(1, rest.length)
            var part = rest.substring(0, take)
            val amp = part.lastIndexOf('&')
            if (amp >= 0 && part.indexOf(';', amp) < 0 && part.length > amp + 1) {
                part = part.substring(0, amp)
            }
            if (part.isNotEmpty()) chunks += part.trim()
            rest.delete(0, part.length.coerceAtLeast(1))
        }
        return chunks.filter(String::isNotBlank)
    }
```

Careful: `rest.delete(0, part.length)` with part.length ≥ 1 when take ≥ 1 — but if take becomes 0 and rest non-empty, take=1 → part = 1 char (maybe '&' → amp=0, part.length(1) > 0+1 false → keep). part non-empty. OK. Also guard delete with coerceAtLeast(1) to avoid infinite loop on empty part.

Edge: if `part` after amp-cut is empty (e.g. part="&...")? part.length > amp + 1 ensures at least one char after '&', so cutting gives 1+ chars. OK, part non-empty.

