Manifest is fine. Now fix the ordering in `grantProjection`.

Let me edit: move `ensureForeground(true)` to the top of the try, before getMediaProjection. And in catch, call ensureForeground(false).

Current:
```kotlin
    private fun grantProjection(resultCode: Int, data: Intent) {
        try {
            val mpm = getSystemService(Context.MEDIA_PROJECTION_SERVICE) as MediaProjectionManager
            val mp = mpm.getMediaProjection(resultCode, data)
            if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= 29) {
                ...
            }
            projection = mp
            projectionGranted = true
            bindProjection(mp)
            ensureForeground(true)
        } catch (e: Exception) {
            Toast.makeText(this, "Захват экрана не запустился: ${e.message}", Toast.LENGTH_LONG).show()
        }
    }
```

New:
```kotlin
    private fun grantProjection(resultCode: Int, data: Intent) {
        try {
            // Android 14 требует, чтобы foreground-сервис с типом mediaProjection
            // уже работал ДО getMediaProjection()/createVirtualDisplay(); иначе
            // система сразу останавливает проекцию (onStop → «захват выключен»).
            ensureForeground(true)
            val mpm = getSystemService(Context.MEDIA_PROJECTION_SERVICE) as MediaProjectionManager
            val mp = mpm.getMediaProjection(resultCode, data)
            if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= 29) {
                ... callback ...
            }
            projection = mp
            projectionGranted = true
            bindProjection(mp)
        } catch (e: Exception) {
            ensureForeground(false)
            Toast.makeText(this, "Захват экрана не запустился: ${e.message}", Toast.LENGTH_LONG).show()
        }
    }
```

Wait, but ACTION_PROJECTION handler calls grantProjection then immediately scanOnce()/startAutoRead(). scanOnce posts to ocrHandler. bindProjection runs synchronously in grantProjection (main thread), so by the time scanOnce runs, reader is set. Good.

But now, `bindProjection` posts on failure; fine.

Also — the `onStartCommand` for ACTION_PROJECTION already called `ensureForeground(projectionGranted)`? No, ACTION_PROJECTION doesn't call ensureForeground before. Actually the CaptureConsentActivity calls `startForegroundService(this)` (ACTION_START) then `startService(s)` ACTION_PROJECTION. The first sets foreground with projectionGranted=false (mediaPlayback only). Then grantProjection upgrades to mediaProjection type. Good.

Let me make the edit.

Also, there might be an additional issue: `getMediaProjection` must be called after the service is foreground with the type. We now ensure that.

However, one more subtlety: `ensureForeground(true)` calls startForeground with MEDIA_PROJECTION type. But at this point, has the app obtained the media projection permission? The type permission FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MEDIA_PROJECTION is normal, no runtime grant. But Android may require that a projection consent token exists? I don't think startForeground checks that. It should be fine — v1.5 called ensureForeground(true) after getMediaProjection and it worked. So the type declaration alone is fine.

Let me apply the edit.

