Now, there's another consideration: the user says "pressing scan does nothing". Let me trace the ACTION_SCAN_ONCE path when projectionGranted=false.

`CaptureConsentActivity.request(this, "scan")` → starts CaptureConsentActivity → onCreate → ask() → startActivityForResult(createScreenCaptureIntent()). This should show the system consent dialog.

Hmm, but why "nothing"? Let me reconsider: maybe after onStop (projection stopped), when the user taps scan, CaptureConsentActivity is launched but the system doesn't show the dialog because... Actually on Android 14, if a projection session was just stopped by the system, re-requesting should work.

Alternatively, "и ничего" might refer to the notification action "OCR скан" which sends ACTION_SCAN_ONCE via PendingIntent.getService. If projectionGranted=false, it requests consent. But PendingIntent.getService starting an activity... From a PendingIntent service start, the service calls CaptureConsentActivity.request → startActivity with NEW_TASK. Should work if the app has background activity start permission — Android 10+ restricts background activity starts! A foreground service CAN start activities? Actually, background activity launch restrictions: apps in the background cannot start activities. A foreground service is considered foreground and CAN start activities in some cases, but Android 14 tightened this. Hmm.

But the user taps the on-screen "Скан" button (in the overlay panel), which runs inside the service directly (not via PendingIntent), and the overlay is a foreground service — starting CaptureConsentActivity from there should be allowed since the app has a foreground service and SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW (which grants background activity start exemption!). SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW permission gives the app the ability to start activities from the background. So that's fine.

OK, the primary fix (ordering) should make the projection not stop, so the user won't see "захват выключен" at all. Let me also double check: after my reorder, does `bindProjection` still possibly fail? With FGS type set first, createVirtualDisplay should succeed.

Let me also reconsider: is there any chance `screenSize()` returns 0 in bindProjection from the service context, making ImageReader.newInstance(0,0,...) throw? If `wm.currentWindowMetrics.bounds` returns 0 for a service... Possible on some devices/API levels. Let me guard: if s.x<=0 || s.y<=0, fall back to display metrics.

Actually `screenSize()` for a service: `WindowManager.getCurrentWindowMetrics()` — the WindowManager obtained from a Service is a "window context"? Service context is not a visual context; `getCurrentWindowMetrics` may throw or return the default display metrics. Hmm. In practice, many apps use it from services. But to be safe, let me make screenSize robust with a fallback.

Let me improve screenSize:
```kotlin
private fun screenSize(): Point {
    return try {
        if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= 30) {
            val b = wm.currentWindowMetrics.bounds
            if (b.width() > 0 && b.height() > 0) return Point(b.width(), b.height())
        }
        val p = Point()
        @Suppress("DEPRECATION")
        wm.defaultDisplay.getRealSize(p)
        if (p.x <= 0 || p.y <= 0) {
            val dm = resources.displayMetrics
            p.set(dm.widthPixels, dm.heightPixels)
        }
        p
    } catch (e: Exception) {
        val dm = resources.displayMetrics
        Point(dm.widthPixels, dm.heightPixels)
    }
}
```

